    {
      "group": 42,
      "index": 0,
      "claim": "\\paragraph{Cell-level agreement and seed noise.} Table~\\ref{tab:geom} now carries the regenerated values, so the question is how stable they are across draws. 18 of the 25 cells fall inside the three-seed range of the measurement and do not exceed observed re-draw variation. Across the four rectangle arms the \\emph{loss slots} spread is smaller than the per-arm seed spread (Table~\\ref{tab:geomprov}), so that column's ordering carries no information and no claim in this paper depends on it. The rank order of the arms on anatomy hidden and on purity is identical across all three draws, which is what the rank correlations in the main text rely on.",
